@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Set up your database"; }
<section class="panel narrow"><span class="eyebrow">LET’S GET YOU STARTED</span><h1>Your booking system is ready for its database.</h1><p>The app could not connect to the booking database. Follow these steps on your computer:</p><ol><li>Open SQL Server Management Studio and connect to your SQL Server.</li><li>Open <code>Database/Setup.sql</code> from the project and execute the entire script.</li><li>Check <code>ConnectionStrings:conn</code> in <code>Bus_Booking_System/appsettings.json</code>. It currently targets <code>.\SQLEXPRESS</code> and database <code>BusBooking</code>.</li><li>Reload this page, then create your account.</li></ol><a class="button" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Try connection again</a><p class="muted mt-3">The README explains how to grant your account administrator access.</p></section>
